## Tech stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Language | Python 3.14 |
| Env + deps | uv (interpreter, venv, lockfile) |
| Tests | pytest + pytest-mock |
| Lint + format | ruff |
| Type checking | mypy `--strict` (the build gate) |
| Platform | local tools only, no containers |

## Platform rules

- **No containers.** No Containerfile, no Dockerfile, no Testcontainers. Build,
  test, and check on the local machine with `uv run ...`.
- **No services, no observability.** This is an importable library/CLI, not a
  traced service.
- **Editors: VS Code or PyCharm** (CLI-driven). Every action is a `uv run` command.

## How to set up

```bash
uv sync                               # create the env from pyproject + uv.lock
./scripts/check-prereqs.sh            # verify the toolchain
```

## How to test

```bash
uv run pytest                         # run the suite
uv run pytest -k {{FILTER}}           # a subset by name
```

## How to check

```bash
uv run ruff check .                   # lint
uv run ruff format --check .          # format gate
uv run mypy --strict src tests        # type gate (fails on untyped / Any leaks)
```

## Key file locations

```
pyproject.toml            ← uv project + [tool.pytest] + [tool.ruff] + [tool.mypy]
uv.lock                   ← pinned, reproducible environment (committed)
src/{{PACKAGE}}/          ← importable package code (src layout)
tests/test_*.py           ← pytest + pytest-mock, no services
scripts/check-prereqs.sh  ← toolchain gate (exits non-zero if missing)
```

## Conventions

- **mypy `--strict` is the gate.** New code is fully typed from the first line; a
  possible-`None` or an untyped function fails the type check, not a test.
- Pin dependencies in `pyproject.toml` and commit `uv.lock`. No floating specifiers,
  no prereleases.
- Prefer `Protocol`/duck typing over interface hierarchies; dataclasses, context
  managers, decorators, `functools.singledispatch`, generators, callables. When a
  GoF pattern is redundant in Python, say so rather than reproduce it.
- Mock collaborators with `pytest-mock`'s `mocker` fixture. Run
  `lgtm-idiomatic-review` (Python rules) before release.
